from collections import defaultdict

def group_anagrams(words):
    groups = defaultdict(list)
    for word in words:
        key = "".join(sorted(word.lower()))
        groups[key].append(word)
    return list(groups.values())
```
The grouping key is the word's lowercase letters sorted into a canonical order. Anagrams contain the same letters with the same counts, so they produce the same key.

